title: The Spandau Arsenal
subtitle: The occupiers have more courage than rifles.
view-if: crisis_january = 1 and jan_arms_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; jan_arms_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Spandau Arsenal

The men in the *Vorwärts* building have rifles, a few machine guns and not much ammunition. In Spandau, workers at the arsenal say the depots could be opened. Others in the party want the weapons kept back for a better day.

- @seize: Seize the arsenal.
- @share: Share out what we have among the occupiers.
- @hide: Hide the guns for another day.

@seize
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's answer. Better armed fighters, and a harder blow from Noske.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.crisis_momentum += 10;
Q.red_guards_arms += 15;
Q.red_guards_strength += 1;
Q.repression += 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

A column of Spandau workers comes into the city on lorries, rifles stacked behind the cabs. The government calls it proof of a Bolshevik plot.

@share
subtitle: The Left Radicals' way: every factory arms itself. A little stronger, a little more chaotic.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 4; red_guards_strength += 1; ultraleft_satisfaction += 5; lean_ultraleft += 1

Rifles pass from hand to hand in the courtyards. Nobody keeps a list.

@hide
subtitle: The Spartacist caution. The occupiers feel abandoned; the weapons survive.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum -= 5; red_guards_arms += 8; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 4; lean_luxemburgist += 1; lux_risk -= 3

Crates of rifles disappear into allotment sheds in Neukölln and Lichtenberg. They will be needed again.
